      "side": 1,
      "message": "Yes, but this is loading a full module that is only bloating android code.\n\nTARGET_FLOSS should be remove everywhere in order to:\n* Not have any logical difference between android and floss\n* abstract library into build time dependency instead of inlining it (like here)\n\nSo a good way to do that would be to have a library for floss only, that when build expose the exact same API as the android system property library.\n\nThe whole gd sysprop_module should than be put into that and provided at build time.\n\nThen from a code point of view, we \"just get a sysprop\" and it is provided whatever the os it is run on.\n\n\nOf course... this is very easy to say, and take a lot more effort to implement.",
      "parentUuid": "cec965a2_09e48bf3",
